---
title: "4 · Prepare the contract"
description: Choose the client, the signatory, the issuing entity, the language and the format.
sidebar:
  order: 5
  label: "4 · Prepare the contract"
---

**Who:** the person in charge. **Where:** the opportunity › **Contract** tab › step 1 **Prepare**.

## Client

Choose **Company** or **Individual**.

- **Company:** the UEN and the address come from the company's CRM record. Pick the **Client signatory** from the company's contacts. If the services are for another company, choose it under **Company the services are for**.
- **Individual:** the details you enter are saved as a person under CRM **People**.

{% aside type="note" title="The signatory must be linked to the company" %}
The client signatory must be a current contact of the company in CRM, for example a director. If the list is empty, first link the person to the company in CRM.
{% /aside %}

## Contract

Choose the country (the opportunity's country by default), the **Issuing entity**, the **Language** and the **Format** (engagement letter, quotation or VIP contract). Together they select the template.

Only combinations with a registered template are offered. If the country has none, the page says so; ask a tenant admin to register one (see [1 · Contract templates](/en/crm/templates/)).

{% screenshot id="crm/prepare-form" caption="The Prepare step: client, signatory, issuing entity, language and format." /%}

{% screenshot id="crm/prepare-entities" caption="Only issuing entities with a template are offered." /%}

## Services and prices

The services and prices are read from the **Services** tab. To change them, select **Edit in Services**.
